---
import { pricing, RATES_EFFECTIVE } from '@/data/pricing';

const premium = pricing.double.academic - pricing.double.full;
---

<section class="border-y border-border bg-muted/30">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-2xl reveal">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-primary">How the lease works</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl">
        Priced against an apartment. Without the apartment.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
        The rates above are twelve-month rates, the same basis a Westwood apartment quotes on. The
        difference is what the number covers. An apartment arrives empty, with utilities, internet,
        and renters insurance still to sort out and a deposit due before you have moved a single box.
        Here one figure covers the room, the furniture, utilities, WiFi, laundry, and the shared
        kitchen and study spaces.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 reveal">
      <div class="border-2 border-primary bg-card p-7">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-primary">Full year · best rate</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-card-foreground">Twelve months</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
          Your room stays yours through the summer, for research, an internship, or simply because
          you would rather not move twice. This is the lowest monthly rate we offer and the one to
          hold up against an apartment listing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="border border-border bg-card p-7">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted-foreground">
          Academic year · add ${premium} a month
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-card-foreground">
          Mid-September to mid-June
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
          Only need the school year? Take the nine-month term, leave after spring finals, and owe
          nothing over the summer — no rent on an empty room and no subletter to find in April.
          Almost no apartment near campus will offer you that at any price.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 max-w-3xl text-xs leading-5 text-muted-foreground reveal">
      For agreements beginning {RATES_EFFECTIVE}, covering winter and spring 2027 and carried unchanged into the 2027–28
      academic year — there is no mid-year increase. Rates are per person, per month, and exclude
      the refundable security deposit. Private rooms vary by tier; the rate shown is the starting
      one. Availability changes by lease cycle.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
